<speak>Your objective is to release liquidity for your anticipated personal commitments while reducing exposure to holdings vulnerable to adverse market developments. That is the objective I am working with for this review. For Orion Global Income Fund, rising market interest rates can reduce the value of the bonds it holds and bring down its unit value. You could lose some or all of the capital you have invested, and selling may crystallise a loss. Are you willing to accept investment losses, including realising a loss on this sale to meet your liquidity needs?</speak>